  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Express $\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}\u2061{36}^{\u2218}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}(1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061{36}^{\u2218})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={36}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061{36}^{\u2218} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {36}^{\u2218})=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{72}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}(1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061{36}^{\u2218})=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{72}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
